  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nitration of aniline gives otho, para and meta nitro anilines but para and also meta are formed in significant amounts,</p><p>meta&nbsp;isomer is formed due to the formation of anilinium ion,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0095_a5ccd397a7bb.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 181px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is strong acid, hence</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0095_1e0b24ab2b07.png\" style=\"width: 430px; height: 125px;\" /></p>"
